A||||8||Philphine||rear deck vents||||1||
Z||000000||Philphine||03-11-2001||11:47 AM||||<BR>i'm gonna take the under side grill work off the the side vents of my '87 coupe for whatever extra cooling i might get and to make them easier to clean. i've heard of it being done but i'm wondering if i need to worry about my battery getting the extra rain exposure.||||reg||1
Z||000001||theogre||03-11-2001||01:50 PM||||I imagine you have the samped metal louver sheet. Removing it should help. (No I don't know exactly how much.) You probably want to replace it with some 1/4 galvanized masonry screen. that will keep leaves and things out that could start a fire.<P>The battery doesn't care about water. You want to make sure the battery terminals are cleaned and greased. I use Dielectric on them. It will repel the water and won't easily wash off. Silicone brake grease works as well but looks bad.<P>have a read of my heat management section in the cave if you haven't already.||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroJoe||03-12-2001||10:28 AM||||I did mine the other night.  There are 7 rivets to drill out, took me about 5 minutes to do both.  I then painted them satin black, and covered them with many coats of gloss polyurethane.  They look great so far, but I havent had the chance to see what they look like on the car.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||qwikgta||03-12-2001||10:27 PM||||Next time you find a pair of 84 covers, buy them, they work great at covering up when it looks like rain outside.  Thats what I do, just dont forget to swap them back before you hit the road.  Take the factory screws off and just swap out your "Drilled out" originals, also helps if you get swap out the driver side screws with the easy ones on the battery side.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>QWIKGTA<BR>88 T-Top coupe<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||03-13-2001||07:57 PM||||I use the old style 85-86 with the hex punched screen under them on mine. except in winter, then I put the OE ones back to keep crap from piling in around the battery. The older ones look better have more air flow than the stamped bottom ones.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Philphine||03-14-2001||10:10 PM||||just drilled them out. it looks like i can drill and tap the holes and reattatch them if i want. thanks for the input.||||reg||1
